  "equipment_type": "Sensor (humidity and temperature probe)",
  "applies_to": "Vaisala HMP1/3/4/5/7/8/9, TMP1 and MMP8 probes with the Modbus RTU interface (user guide M212022EN-M).",
  "summary": "The HMP Series are Vaisala HUMICAP humidity and temperature probes for industrial use (MMP8 measures moisture in oil, TMP1 is temperature only). Each probe is a Modbus RTU slave on RS-485. This map covers all measured and calculated humidity parameters, measurement and device status, compensation, purge and filtering settings, serial settings and test registers.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 240,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "The guide numbers registers in decimal starting at 1 and also prints the 0-based hex address used in the request; register number 1 is address 0x0000 on the wire."
  },
  "default_word_order": "CDAB",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "HMP Series with MMP8 and TMP1 User Guide",
    "doc_number": "M212022EN-M",
    "revision_date": "2025-08",
    "url": "https://docs.vaisala.com/r/M212022EN-M/en-US",
    "pages": "Appendix A Modbus reference, pp. 134-147"
  },
  "notes": [
    "All registers are holding registers: read with function 03, write with function 16.",
    "32-bit floats and 32-bit integers put the least significant word at the listed register (CDAB). The guide's data-encoding section covers both formats and its worked read and write examples confirm the order.",
    "Unavailable data reads as quiet NaN (float) or 0x8000 (16-bit integer) rather than an exception.",
    "Which parameters return data depends on the probe: TMP1 is a temperature probe, and MMP8 measures moisture in oil (water activity and ppm).",
    "Integer registers use the scale listed per register (for example raw x 0.01 for RH and temperature).",
    "Register 513 reads 0 when an error is active and 1 when there is none, as printed in the guide.",
    "Error code register 516 is listed as a 32-bit signed integer; it is a sum of the error bits shown.",
    "The T and Td/f measurement status registers (521, 522) share a table cell with the RH status bit list in the guide, so their bits are not repeated here."
  ],
